+	(including spaces) into one argument, and "" gives an empty argument.
+	Backslash has no special meaning, as it is the path separator on TOS.
+	If storage_list is 0, then arguments are only counted.
+	*chars is increased with the number of bytes needed for the arguments (including nulls).
+	Returns the number of arguments (not including argv[0]).
